development.question_text:
This site plan of a rectangular roof is drawn to a scale of $1:400$. If $16$ mm of rain falls on the roof, find the volume of water collected, in litres.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) -- (4.8,0) node[midway, below] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\draw (4.8,0) -- (4.8,3) node[midway, right] {$2.5\text{ cm}$};
\draw (4.8,3) -- (0,3);
\draw (0,3) -- (0,0);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

mastery.question_text:
This site plan of an L-shaped warehouse roof is drawn to a scale of $1:250$. A storm drops $22$ mm of rain on the roof. Find the volume of runoff from the roof, in kilolitres.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4.8,0);
\coordinate (C) at (4.8,1.92);
\coordinate (D) at (3.2,1.92);
\coordinate (E) at (3.2,3.2);
\coordinate (F) at (0,3.2);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, below] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway, right] {$2.4\text{ cm}$};
\draw (C) -- (D) node[midway, above] {$2\text{ cm}$};
\draw (D) -- (E) node[midway, right] {$1.6\text{ cm}$};
\draw (E) -- (F) node[midway, above] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\draw (F) -- (A) node[midway, left] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
